# Install-time configuration for install-macos.py.
# Values here are policy choices, not runtime settings -- runtime config lives
# in config.env under Application Support.

# ── Automatic login ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# An appliance box has to come all the way back to a logged-in GUI session on
# its own after a power cut. Camera capture needs GUI/TCC ancestry, so stopping
# at the login window means no stream until someone types a password.
#
#   kcpassword  Installer prompts for the account password and writes
#               /etc/kcpassword itself (needs sudo). Fully unattended after.
#   guide       Installer never touches the password. It checks whether
#               autologin is on and, if not, opens System Settings and tells
#               the operator what to flip -- then verifies it took.
#   skip        Do nothing; assume it is handled out of band.
#
# `guide` is implemented and ready. It is not the default only because these
# boxes are provisioned unattended; switch to it if handling the account
# password in the installer ever becomes unacceptable.
AUTOLOGIN_MODE=kcpassword

# ── Code signing ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Empty means ad-hoc (`codesign --sign -`), which is the permanent state for
# this fleet by decision -- no Apple Developer Program membership.
#
# Consequence, so it is not a surprise later: an ad-hoc signature has no Team
# ID, so TCC pins its grants to a literal cdhash. Any rebuild changes that
# hash, which silently voids the camera and microphone approvals and makes the
# operator re-approve them. Reboots are unaffected; only reinstalls/updates.
#
# Setting this to a "Developer ID Application: ..." identity, plus a notarytool
# profile below, is all that is needed to get stable grants and no Gatekeeper
# prompt. The build path is already wired for it.
CODESIGN_IDENTITY=

# notarytool keychain profile name (see `xcrun notarytool store-credentials`).
# Ignored unless CODESIGN_IDENTITY is also set -- notarization requires a
# Developer ID signature; an ad-hoc binary is rejected by the service.
NOTARIZE_PROFILE=
